[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hey all, I'm pretty new to Lean and trying to learn. My background is in Category Theory, and eventually I'd like to be able to use Lean 4 to formalize my Master's thesis, but before I do that, I thought I'd try to formalize / contribute some other results. But I had a few questions.</p>\n<p>1. If I want to contribute a result that's in Wikidata (e.x. <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q15809744\">https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q15809744</a>) but not in the 1000+ theorems, where (if anywhere) would I contribute that in mathlib?</p>\n<p>2. I found a previous formalization of Lawvere's Fixed point theorem in the <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/archive/stream/217875-Is-there-code-for-X%3F/topic/Lawvere.20fixed.20point.20theorem.html#441321736\">zulip archives</a> and I'm trying to update it to work with the latest mathlib for potential contribution. Here is what I have so far (just trying to state some preliminaries for the theorem):</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CategoryTheory</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Limits</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Shapes</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">FiniteProducts</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CategoryTheory</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Limits</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MonoidalClosed</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">universe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Category</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">MonoidalCategory</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">][</span><span class=\"n\">HasFiniteProducts</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">MonoidalClosed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">weakly_point_surjective</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Category</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">MonoidalCategory</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">HasFiniteProducts</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">MonoidalClosed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟶</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟹</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">):</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟶</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊤_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟶</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊤_</span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟶</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">prod</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">rightUnitor</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">inv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">uncurry</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fixed_point_property</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Category</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">MonoidalCategory</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">HasFiniteProducts</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">MonoidalClosed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">):</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟶</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊤_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟶</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- **Lawvere’s Fixed‑Point Theorem**. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lawvere_fixed_point</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟶</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⇒</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WeaklyPointSurjective</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">FixedPointProperty</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Basically so far I've just updated the code from the archive to use up-to-date imports and to remove deprecated typeclasses. Yet this seems to not work in modern lean for some reason and I'm not sure why?</p>\n<p>The big issue seems to be that the ⇒ notation for expontential objects is not working anymore. Does anyone know what the proper syntax is in the latest mathlib?</p>",
        "id": 592568949,
        "sender_full_name": "Nathan BeDell",
        "timestamp": 1777822175
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You want to do <code>open scoped CartesianClosed</code> to get the notation in<br>\nAlso, the way of saying that <code>C</code> is a cartesian closed category is <code>(C: Type*) [Category* C] [CartesianMonoidalCategory C] [MonoidalClosed C]</code>.</p>",
        "id": 592572360,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Carlier",
        "timestamp": 1777824951
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>in addition to what Robin said, you may be using the wrong notation... in your code you wrote <code>⇒</code> but the arrow for exponential objects is <code>⟹</code></p>",
        "id": 592594082,
        "sender_full_name": "Matt Diamond",
        "timestamp": 1777841925
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>you can type it using <code>\\nattrans</code>, <code>\\nat_trans</code>, or <code>\\==&gt;</code></p>",
        "id": 592594188,
        "sender_full_name": "Matt Diamond",
        "timestamp": 1777842026
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"684366\">@Edward van de Meent</span> what did I do</p>",
        "id": 592601723,
        "sender_full_name": "Matt Diamond",
        "timestamp": 1777849537
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Nothing, I was just disappointed in the naming of the shortcut</p>",
        "id": 592602527,
        "sender_full_name": "Edward van de Meent",
        "timestamp": 1777850337
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Since afaik that notation isn't used for natural transformations in lean</p>",
        "id": 592602551,
        "sender_full_name": "Edward van de Meent",
        "timestamp": 1777850364
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It's nothing personal</p>",
        "id": 592602566,
        "sender_full_name": "Edward van de Meent",
        "timestamp": 1777850384
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>lol no worries, that did seem weird to me too... maybe a holdover from a past version of Lean, who knows</p>",
        "id": 592602601,
        "sender_full_name": "Matt Diamond",
        "timestamp": 1777850415
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think it's a hold over from (iirc) copying them over from some other proof assistent, I think Agda maybe?</p>",
        "id": 592602754,
        "sender_full_name": "Edward van de Meent",
        "timestamp": 1777850549
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Similar to how <code>\\8&lt;</code> was a shortcut for some scissors-symbol which was never used in actual lean code</p>",
        "id": 592602830,
        "sender_full_name": "Edward van de Meent",
        "timestamp": 1777850641
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"1076193\">@Nathan BeDell</span> another note: I think you're supposed to use <code>𝟙_ C</code> instead of <code>⊤_ C</code> for the terminal object when you're working with cartesian monoidal categories</p>",
        "id": 592604134,
        "sender_full_name": "Matt Diamond",
        "timestamp": 1777852000
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>also, I'm not a category theorist so take this with a huge grain of salt, but I wonder if it might be better to define weakly point surjective like this:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">weakly_point_surjective</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟶</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟹</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟶</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">𝟙</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟶</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">𝟙</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟶</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">),</span>\n<span class=\"n\">lift</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ihom</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">app</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 592604579,
        "sender_full_name": "Matt Diamond",
        "timestamp": 1777852422
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"380294\">@Matt Diamond</span> - Good catch! I actually just figured that bit out myself earlier. I have an actual statement of the theorem that compiles now:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CategoryTheory</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Limits</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Shapes</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">FiniteProducts</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CategoryTheory</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Limits</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MonoidalClosed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SemiCartesianMonoidalCategory</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MonoidalCategory</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">scoped</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CartesianClosed</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">universe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Category</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CartesianMonoidalCategory</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">MonoidalClosed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">weakly_point_surjective</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟶</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟹</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">):</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟶</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">𝟙</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟶</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">𝟙</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟶</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ρ_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">inv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">uncurry</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fixed_point_property</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Category</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CartesianMonoidalCategory</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">MonoidalClosed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">):</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟶</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">𝟙</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟶</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- **Lawvere’s Fixed‑Point Theorem**. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lawvere_fixed_point</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Category</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CartesianMonoidalCategory</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">MonoidalClosed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟶</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟹</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">weakly_point_surjective</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">fixed_point_property</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 592604628,
        "sender_full_name": "Nathan BeDell",
        "timestamp": 1777852477
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That =&gt; v.s. ==&gt; thing is something I ran into as well. Took me forever to figure out there was a distinction.</p>",
        "id": 592604757,
        "sender_full_name": "Nathan BeDell",
        "timestamp": 1777852629
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>And yeah, I found the natural transformation naming confusing too.</p>",
        "id": 592604770,
        "sender_full_name": "Nathan BeDell",
        "timestamp": 1777852652
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>What I'm having problems with now is that the proof itself uses the diagonal morphism <code>diag : X ⟶ X ⨯ X</code>,  but I actually need it to be <code>X⟶ X ⊗ X</code>.</p>\n<p>I assume I need to use <code>tensorProductIsBinaryProduct</code> or something maybe?</p>",
        "id": 592608546,
        "sender_full_name": "Nathan BeDell",
        "timestamp": 1777853610
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>maybe <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Monoidal/Cartesian/Basic.html#CategoryTheory.CartesianMonoidalCategory.lift\">CategoryTheory.CartesianMonoidalCategory.lift</a>?</p>",
        "id": 592609478,
        "sender_full_name": "Matt Diamond",
        "timestamp": 1777853781
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>also curious if you had any thoughts on my comment re: the definition of weakly point surjective</p>",
        "id": 592609743,
        "sender_full_name": "Matt Diamond",
        "timestamp": 1777853829
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I have a proof of Lawvere's Fixed-Point theorem using that definition but it's relatively short (like 6 lines or so) which makes me wonder if perhaps it assumes too much</p>",
        "id": 592610277,
        "sender_full_name": "Matt Diamond",
        "timestamp": 1777853929
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'll be honest, I'm still trying to parse your version and understand the difference. <span aria-label=\"sweat smile\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f605\" role=\"img\" title=\"sweat smile\">:sweat_smile:</span> </p>\n<p>I literally just started seriously learning Lean 4 (trying to actually work examples, not just reading docs) yesterday.</p>",
        "id": 592610988,
        "sender_full_name": "Nathan BeDell",
        "timestamp": 1777854057
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It's been awhile since I've actually read Lawvere's paper, but I think it was a pretty simple proof, so I don't think six lines sounds too far off to me.</p>",
        "id": 592611237,
        "sender_full_name": "Nathan BeDell",
        "timestamp": 1777854102
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I can share my version if you'd like, though it's probably better for you to try to work it out yourself</p>",
        "id": 592611469,
        "sender_full_name": "Matt Diamond",
        "timestamp": 1777854147
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah, that's true. I'll work from your definition and see if I can formalize a similarly short proof.</p>",
        "id": 592612178,
        "sender_full_name": "Nathan BeDell",
        "timestamp": 1777854367
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I did find the original paper again, and it is a very short proof (page 5): <a href=\"http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/reprints/articles/15/tr15.pdf\">http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/reprints/articles/15/tr15.pdf</a></p>",
        "id": 592612441,
        "sender_full_name": "Nathan BeDell",
        "timestamp": 1777854440
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Actually, if I understand it correctly, I think your definition is closer to how Lawvere defines it in his paper. I'm not sure why the one from the archive used <code>uncurry</code>.</p>",
        "id": 592613006,
        "sender_full_name": "Nathan BeDell",
        "timestamp": 1777854893
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>on a side note, if you're extremely new to Lean and looking for basic exercises, you could also try to prove a very simple version of Lawvere's Theorem in the type-theoretical context:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">universe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lawvere</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Surjective</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 592613074,
        "sender_full_name": "Matt Diamond",
        "timestamp": 1777854966
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(though that one may be a little <em>too</em> easy, idk...)</p>",
        "id": 592613173,
        "sender_full_name": "Matt Diamond",
        "timestamp": 1777855062
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"1076193\">Nathan BeDell</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Exponential.20Object.20in.20Category.20Theory/near/592608546\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>What I'm having problems with now is that the proof itself uses the diagonal morphism <code>diag : X ⟶ X ⨯ X</code>,  but I actually need it to be <code>X⟶ X ⊗ X</code>.</p>\n<p>I assume I need to use <code>tensorProductIsBinaryProduct</code> or something maybe?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>You can also use <code>lift</code> with the identity twice</p>\n<p>Most of the time when working with Cartesian monoidal categories you really want to avoid mixing the binary product from the <code>HasLimit</code> API with the tensor product, and instead work exclusively with the tensor product.</p>",
        "id": 592630287,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Carlier",
        "timestamp": 1777868809
    }
]